values ('c7d8e9f0-1a2b-4d36-9f56-6a7b8c9d0e66', 'american-literature-i-pre-1865', 'American Literature I (Pre-1865)', 'American Literature I (Pre-1865) surveys literature in and about North America from Indigenous oral traditions and colonial encounter through Puritanism, revolution, early national print culture, slavery and abolition, Transcendentalism, American Romanticism, women writers, poetry, and antebellum politics. The course treats literature as an archive of contested nation formation: a record of sovereignty, empire, faith, race, gender, labor, environment, citizenship, and literary experiment. Students practice close reading, historical contextualization, archive use, and scholarly argument.');

